{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111965","id":2941758984,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6vV64I","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111965/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111965/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/05c33acbb1e7189719d1edd6105cbb23065bdd9d","number":111965,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Make `memnew(RefCounted)` return `Ref`, to improve ownership safety","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR improves `RefCounted` ownership semantics for newly created objects, preventing potential crashes and other footguns at build time.\r\n\r\n## Background\r\n\r\nWhen `memnew` initializes `RefCounted` subclasses, they start with an (effective) allocation count of 0.\r\n\r\nThis creates two ownership related problems:\r\n\r\n- When stored as `RefCounted *` initially, some code may increase and later decrease the refcount (e.g. when passing as `Variant`). This destructs the object, because the refcount is decreased to 0. The actual owner's `RefCounted *` will be a dangling pointer. The owner should have stored `Ref<RefCounted>` instead.\r\n- When in the `postinitialize_handler` / `NOTIFICATION_POSTINITIALIZE`, `RefCounted` objects still have an allocation count of 0, because the caller of `memnew` didn't claim a reference yet. If the allocation count is increased and later decreased during this function, the object will unexpectedly destruct (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108395).\r\n\r\nThe ideal (only?) way to fix this is to start `RefCounted` with a refcount of 1. The `memnew` caller must take ownership of the refcount after the call. This just means we return `Ref` from `memnew`. Most callers already store the result in a `Ref`, so they are compatible with this change.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nImplementing the change was fairly straight-forward; I add and specialize `memnew_result_t` such that for `RefCounted` types, `memnew` returns `Ref<T>`.\r\n\r\nThe rest of the changes are fixing current ownership problems. Mostly, it just involves changing `T *` to `Ref<T>`. It has some inherent risk, but I don't think it's huge.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":